arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-oneplus-kebab: full hardware enablement

Bring the kebab device tree from the framework baseline to the state
verified on the running device:
- NFC (SN100T): split enable/firmware GPIOs (gpio83 VEN, gpio110 FIRM)
- QCA6390: standalone qca6390-pmu node with AON LDO; qca639x keeps the
  verified supply rails (vddpmu on s6a) and loses the baseline's new
  pinctrl-driven wlan-en in favour of the wlan-bt-enable GPIO hog on
  tlmm 20 (WLAN only); pcie1 clkreq pinctrl group removed (gpio83
  conflict); bluetooth loses its pinctrl/enable-gpios and is fed from
  the PMU AON LDO instead of the qca639x power domain. BT enable
  (tlmm 21) is driven by the PMU power sequencer (bt-enable-gpios +
  bt_en pinctrl on the PMU node, wired like qrb5165-rb5): with the
  enable hogged high the controller could never power-cycle, so any
  re-setup desynced its UART and wedged it (found on run #7,
  2026-11-06; the hog keeps tlmm 20 only - WLAN has no pwrseq
  consumer on this board)
- PCIe0 PHY: drop the baseline's power-domains = <&qca639x> from
  &pcie0_phy. In this kernel build nothing registers that power
  domain, so the PHY probe deadlocks waiting for it and the QCA6390
  never enumerates (no WiFi; found on the run-#6 image, 2026-11-06).
  The PHY runs on its direct vdda supplies, as in the reference tree
- Panel: MDSS/DSI + Samsung AMB655X panel, panel AVDD fixed
  regulator, panel pinctrl states, dispcc and GPU enabled (zap
  firmware path set)
- USB: USB3 unlocked (QMP PHY, OTG role switch, Type-C connector
  with fixed 5V/3A dual-role PDOs, PM8150B Type-C enabled)
- PON: mode-bootloader / mode-recovery for reboot-to-mode support
- PM8150B charger + VBUS regulator enabled; battery monitoring
- Haptics enabled with boost GPIO and 150 Hz play rate

Rebased onto the linux-6.18.y (f45ed76) + in-tree series baseline of
2026-11-05; compiled DTB verified against the reference device tree
with only the two ruled removals (ramoops node, hardcoded BT address)
and upstream 6.18.60 dtsi drift (venus OPP table, mmcx power domain)
remaining. The BT-enable pwrseq delta was
compiled and DTB-diffed on 2026-11-06 (delta limited to the hog
gpios/line-name and the PMU bt-enable-gpios/pinctrl).

- BQ25980 charge pump: compatible ti,bq25980 -> ti,bq2597x-standalone.
  The baseline string matches no driver (the in-tree bq2597x charger
  driver, CONFIG_CHARGER_BQ25970=y, binds only the ti,bq2597x-*
  compatibles), so the pump stayed unmanaged and uninspectable.
